ge, and tests to run. If nothing is assigned to me, suggest three small open tickets that fit this repo and recommend one to start with."},{"pluginKey":"datadog","title":"Investigate errors","subtitle":"Find the top production errors and where they start in the code","prompt":"Pull the most frequent production errors from the last 24 hours, group them by likely root cause, and trace the top one to the code in this repo that throws it. Tell me what you'd check or fix first. If it's quiet, summarize overall service health instead."},{"pluginKey":"slack","title":"Catch up on Slack","subtitle":"Catch up on mentions and threads waiting on a reply","prompt":"Summarize my unread mentions and the threads where someone is waiting on me. For anything code-related, point me to the relevant part of this repo, and draft a short reply I can edit for the two most urgent ones."},{"pluginKey":"supabase","title":"Review your schema","subtitle":"Review the database schema for performance and security issues","prompt":"Use the connected Supabase project and this repo to review the database design. Explain how the main tables relate, check for missing indexes, risky RLS policies, and schema patterns that could cause bugs or slow queries. Suggest the top three improvements and include the SQL or migration I should review before applying."}],"Product Manager":[{"pluginKey":"jira","title":"Draft a spec","subtitle":"Draft a product spec from an active project","prompt":"Find active projects in the connected workspace, pick the one with the most recent activity, and draft a one-page product spec from its issues and docs: the problem, requirements, open questions, and anything ambiguous or contradictory. Flag assumptions the project relies on but never states."},{"pluginKey":"amplitude","title":"Analyze usage","subtitle":"Summarize adoption and drop-off for a feature","prompt":"Look at recent usage in Amplitude and summarize adoption and drop-off for a feature: who's picking it up, where people fall out of the flow, and how that changed over the last 30 days. Ask me which feature to look at, or if one stands out in the data, start there and tell me why."},{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Synthesize feedback","subtitle":"Turn scattered feedback into ranked product themes","prompt":"Search my Notion workspace for customer feedback, research notes, and meeting notes from the last quarter. Synthesize them into ranked themes with rough frequency, and draft a short problem brief for the top theme. Cite which notes each theme came from."},{"pluginKey":"figma","title":"Prototype a mock","subtitle":"Turn a mock into a clickable prototype","prompt":"I want to turn a Figma mock into a clickable prototype I can share. Ask me to paste a link to the frame, then build it as a working page and tell me how to view it in the browser."}],"Designer":[{"pluginKey":"figma","title":"Design to code","subtitle":"Turn a design frame into working, clickable code","prompt":"I want to turn one of my Figma designs into working code. Ask me to paste a link to the frame (or tell me to select it in Figma), then build it faithfully: real layout, real spacing, real text. Show me how to open it in the browser when you're done."},{"pluginKey":"vercel","title":"Publish a prototype","subtitle":"Put the prototype at a live link anyone can open","prompt":"Take the prototype we've been working on and deploy it to Vercel so I get a live URL I can share for feedback. Walk me through any login step, and give me the link when it's up."},{"pluginKey":"linear","title":"Notes to tickets","subtitle":"Turn handoff notes into tickets engineers can pick up","prompt":"Take my rough handoff notes and turn them into clear, scoped Linear tickets: what to build, the states and edge cases, and what \"done\" looks like. I'll paste the notes, or point you at existing tickets to clean up."},{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Feedback to decisions","subtitle":"Turn design feedback into decisions and next steps","prompt":"Search my Notion for recent design critique or feedback notes, and turn them into a short decision doc: what was decided, what's still open, and the next steps with owners. Keep it to one page."}],"Data":[{"pluginKey":"databricks","title":"Query the warehouse","subtitle":"Answer a business question straight from the warehouse","prompt":"I want to answer a question with our warehouse data. Start by listing the schemas and tables so you know what's available, then ask me what question to dig into. Or if you spot an obviously interesting table, propose a question and answer it with a query I can read."},{"pluginKey":"hex","title":"Chart a question","subtitle":"Build a chart from a metric question","prompt":"Help me turn a question into a Hex notebook: the query, a clean chart, and one sentence on what it shows. Ask me what question to start with, or propose one based on what's in the workspace."},{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Write up findings","subtitle":"Summarize an analysis into findings and recommendations","prompt":"Turn this analysis into a decision-ready brief. Include the business question, method, key findings, caveats, recommendation, and next steps. Call out any assumptions or limitations that could change the decision."},{"pluginKey":"jira","title":"Plan a data request","subtitle":"Turn a data request into queries and an analysis plan","prompt":"Find the data request tickets assigned to me in Jira, pick the top one, and break it into an analysis plan: the clarifying questions I should ask, the tables and queries it needs, and what the deliverable should look like. If nothing's assigned to me, grab a recent request from the team queue."}],"Researcher":[{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Synthesize readings","subtitle":"Synthesize saved readings into themes and findings","prompt":"Search my Notion for reading notes and research materials, and synthesize them into a structured summary: the main themes, where sources agree and disagree, and the open questions worth pursuing. Cite which note each claim comes from."},{"pluginKey":"hex","title":"Explore a dataset","subtitle":"Explore a dataset and chart the key result","prompt":"Help me explore a dataset in a Hex notebook: profile what's in it, run the analysis that best answers my question, and produce a publication-clean figure. Ask me which dataset and question to start with."}],"Student":[{"pluginKey":"vercel","title":"Build & publish","subtitle":"Build a web app and publish it live","prompt":"Help build a simple web app and deploy it with a real URL to share. Ask what to make, or suggest three fun ideas that could be finished today. Then build it, deploy it, and provide the live link."},{"pluginKey":"context7","title":"Debug an error","subtitle":"Debug an error and explain why it happened","prompt":"I'll paste an error I'm stuck on (or find one in this project). Fix it using current documentation for the library involved, then explain what actually went wrong in plain language, like a patient tutor. I want to understand it, not just make it go away."},{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Make a study guide","subtitle":"Turn notes into a study guide and practice plan","prompt":"Search my Notion for class notes on a topic (ask me which), and turn them into a study guide: the key concepts in plain language, five practice problems from easy to hard, and a plan for the week before the exam."}],"Educator":[{"pluginKey":"notion","title":"Plan a lesson","subtitle":"Build a lesson plan with examples and exercises","prompt":"Help me plan a lesson. Ask me the topic and level, then draft lecture notes, two worked examples, and three exercises with an answer key, saved as a doc I can edit."},{"pluginKey":"context7","title":"Create an assignment","subtitle":"Create an assignment with starter code and tests","prompt":"Help me create a programming assignment: ask me the topic and level, then generate starter code, hidden tests, and a rubric, using current library versions so nothing is deprec